Trees\/Tree","abstract":[{"text":"A tree: a connected, acyclic undirected graph with at least one vertex, so it has exactly","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"n − 1 edges, no self-loop and no parallel edges. The invariant is the type: every initializer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from unchecked input is failable, and a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cannot be mutated.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Tree","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Tree","kind":"identifier"}]}}}